    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Prompt the AI to show the message `\"Button One was clicked!\"` when Button One is clicked.\r\n\r\n2. Click Button One and check that it works as expected.\r\n\r\n3. Review the code and look for where it\r\n   - selects the button\r\n   - adds an event listener\r\n   - listens for a click\r\n   - changes the message\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n::: details [**🔎 Show me how**]\r\n### **Walkthrough of Exemplar Code**\r\n\r\n#### **1. Selects the Button**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst buttonOne = document.getElementById(\"buttonOne\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis line finds the button in the HTML so the program can interact with it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **2. Selects the Text Area**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst textArea = document.getElementById(\"textArea\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis selects the part of the page that will be updated.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **3. Adds an Event Listener**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nbuttonOne.addEventListener(\"click\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis tells the program to listen for a click on the button.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **4. Event Handler (What Runs)**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n, () => {...}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis function contains the code that runs when the button is clicked.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **5. Updates the Page (Response)**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\ntextArea.textContent = \"Button One was clicked!\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis changes the text on the page when the button is clicked.\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n\r\n",
